IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-13.l4 -- ARTICLE 13 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: INFORMATION TO BE PROVIDED WHERE PERSONAL DATA ARE
-- COLLECTED FROM THE DATA SUBJECT (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 161-178 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the Section 2 heading at
-- 159-160 and the two heading lines of Article 13 at 161-162 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE `Duty outcome` (every duty here has a "where" gate), MAYBE
-- BOOLEAN for the exception, a DEONTIC for each regulative rule.
--
-- WHOSE.  The controller owes the information; the data subject may rely on it (the data subject's claim, Article 13
-- "shall provide the data subject with").
--
-- THE LISTS.  The text lists the information item by item ((a) to (f) of paragraph 1, (a) to (f) of paragraph 2).  Each
-- item is a constructor of `Art 13(1) item of information` or `Art 13(2) item of further information`; the caller
-- states which items the controller PROVIDED and which the data subject ALREADY HAS (paragraph 4: "where and insofar
-- as the data subject already has the information"), and the function decides whether every item that applies has
-- been provided or is already held.  An item with its own "where applicable" or "if any" is required only where the
-- caller says it applies.
--
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulation gives in its own words; NOTHING means
-- it does not answer on these facts.  Never read NOTHING as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 13(1) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller`
    `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative`
    `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer`
    `Art 13(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended`
    `Art 13(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing`
    `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`
    `Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data`
    `Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards`

DECLARE `Art 13(2) item of further information` IS ONE OF
    `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`
    `Art 13(2)(b) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability`
    `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal`
    `Art 13(2)(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`
    `Art 13(2)(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure`
    `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences`

DECLARE `Art 13 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 13(1) provide the data subject with all of the following information`
    `Art 13(2) provide the data subject with the further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing`
    `Art 13(3) provide the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information`

§ `Article 13(1): the information at the time when the data are obtained`

-- src:163 | 1. Where personal data relating to a data subject are collected from the data subject, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with all of the following information:
-- src:164 | (a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative;
-- src:165 | (b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable;
-- src:166 | (c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing;
-- src:167 | (d) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party;
-- src:168 | (e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any;
-- src:169 | (f) where applicable, the fact that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means by which to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.
@ref Art 13(1) chapeau and points (a) to (f) (src:163-169)
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has a representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has designated a data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items of information that the controller provides` IS A LIST OF `Art 13(1) item of information`
      `the items of information that the data subject already has` IS A LIST OF `Art 13(1) item of information`
      `the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 13(1) the controller provides the data subject with all of the following information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where personal data relating to a data subject are collected from the data subject"
        IF NOT (    held `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller`
                AND held `Art 13(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended`
                AND held `Art 13(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing`
                AND (IF `the controller has a representative` THEN held `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `the controller has designated a data protection officer` THEN held `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` THEN held `Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` THEN held `Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN held `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` ELSE TRUE))
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with all of the following information"
        IF NOT (`the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained` OR null `the items of information that the controller provides`)
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject": the items were provided, but not at that time (R4); where the controller provided nothing because the data subject already has everything, nothing is late
        IF `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS NOTHING
           AND NOT (held `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether item (d) is owed ("where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)") is P1's answer, and it does not answer on these facts; every other item that applies has been provided
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is met`
    WHERE
        held item MEANS elem item `the items of information that the controller provides` OR elem item `the items of information that the data subject already has`
    -- (a) "and, where applicable, of the controller's representative", (b) "where applicable", (e) "if any" and (f) "where applicable" are required only where the caller states they apply.
    -- Paragraph 4 is applied item by item: an item the data subject already has is held, whoever provided it ("where and insofar as").

GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 13 action`
`Art 13(1) the controller must provide the data subject with all of the following information at the time when the personal data are obtained` MEANS
    IF `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 13(1) provide the data subject with all of the following information`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the information was not provided at the time when the personal data were obtained"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- "at the time when personal data are obtained": the clock starts at the time of obtaining and the limit is that instant (WITHIN 0, the deadline is inclusive); the other reading, no limit, is listed under "Marginal readings" (fork F13-2)

§ `Article 13(2): the further information`

-- src:170 | 2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing:
-- src:171 | (a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
-- src:172 | (b) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject or to object to processing as well as the right to data portability;
-- src:173 | (c) where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal;
-- src:174 | (d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
-- src:175 | (e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, or a requirement necessary to enter into a contract, as well as whether the data subject is obliged to provide the personal data and of the possible consequences of failure to provide such data;
-- src:176 | (f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved, as well as the significance and the envisaged consequences of such processing for the data subject.
@ref Art 13(2) chapeau and points (a) to (f) (src:170-176)
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items of further information that the controller provides` IS A LIST OF `Art 13(2) item of further information`
      `the items of further information that the data subject already has` IS A LIST OF `Art 13(2) item of further information`
      `the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 13(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1": paragraph 1 is the case of data collected from the data subject, and the pointer has no gate word (ruling (c); fork F13-1)
        IF NOT (    held `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`
           AND held `Art 13(2)(b) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability`
           AND held `Art 13(2)(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`
           AND held `Art 13(2)(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure`
           AND (IF `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` THEN held `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` ELSE TRUE)
           AND (IF `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` THEN held `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` ELSE TRUE))
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing"
        IF NOT (`the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained` OR null `the items of further information that the controller provides`)
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject": the items were provided, but not at that time (R4); where the controller provided nothing because the data subject already has everything, nothing is late
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is met`
    WHERE
        held item MEANS elem item `the items of further information that the controller provides` OR elem item `the items of further information that the data subject already has`
    -- (c) "where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)" and (f) "the existence of automated decision-making ... referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)" are required only where the caller states the fact.
    -- (f): "at least in those cases": the text requires the logic information at least where Article 22(1) and (4) decisions exist and does not say whether it is required for other automated decision-making; the function reads only the named cases (fork F13-3).

GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 13 action`
`Art 13(2) the controller must provide the data subject with the further information at the time when the personal data are obtained` MEANS
    IF `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 13(2) provide the data subject with the further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the further information was not provided at the time when the personal data were obtained"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Article 13(1) and (2): one item at a time`

-- The two functions below ask the question of `Art 13(1)` and `Art 13(2)` for one item named by the caller: is that item owed?
-- They read the same facts as the whole-list functions (the conditional items are owed only where the caller says they apply, paragraph 4 lifts an item the data subject already has), and answer JUST TRUE where the item is owed, JUST FALSE where the text says it is not, NOTHING where P1's answer is missing (R10).
-- src:163 | 1. Where personal data relating to a data subject are collected from the data subject, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with all of the following information:
-- src:164 | (a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative;
-- src:165 | (b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable;
-- src:166 | (c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing;
-- src:167 | (d) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party;
-- src:168 | (e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any;
-- src:169 | (f) where applicable, the fact that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means by which to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.
@ref Art 13(1) item by item (chapeau and points (a) to (f)) (src:163-169)
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS AN `Art 13(1) item of information`
      `the controller has a representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has designated a data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the item of information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) the controller owes the data subject the item of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where personal data relating to a data subject are collected from the data subject"
        IF `the data subject already has the item of information`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information" (Article 13(4))
        IF item EQUALS `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`
           AND `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether item (d) is owed ("where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)") is P1's answer, and it does not answer on these facts
        IF NOT (applies item)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "(a) ... where applicable, of the controller's representative", "(b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable", "(d) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)", "(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any", "(f) where applicable, the fact that the controller intends to transfer personal data": the item is not owed where its condition fails
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        applies i MEANS
            CONSIDER i
            WHEN `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` THEN `the controller has a representative`
            WHEN `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` THEN `the controller has designated a data protection officer`
            WHEN `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` THEN `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            WHEN `Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` THEN `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data`
            WHEN `Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` THEN `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation`
            OTHERWISE TRUE
    -- the controller's own identity, the purposes and the legal basis are owed in every case (no "where applicable" in (a) first limb and (c)).

-- src:170 | 2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing:
-- src:171 | (a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
-- src:172 | (b) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject or to object to processing as well as the right to data portability;
-- src:173 | (c) where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal;
-- src:174 | (d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
-- src:175 | (e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, or a requirement necessary to enter into a contract, as well as whether the data subject is obliged to provide the personal data and of the possible consequences of failure to provide such data;
-- src:176 | (f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved, as well as the significance and the envisaged consequences of such processing for the data subject.
@ref Art 13(2) item by item (chapeau and points (a) to (f)) (src:170-176)
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS AN `Art 13(2) item of further information`
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the item of information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the controller owes the data subject the item of further information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1": paragraph 1 is the case of data collected from the data subject, and the pointer has no gate word (ruling (c); fork F13-1)
        IF `the data subject already has the item of information`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information" (Article 13(4))
        IF NOT (applies item)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "(c) where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent", "(f) the existence of automated decision-making ... referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)": the item is not owed where its condition fails
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        applies i MEANS
            CONSIDER i
            WHEN `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` THEN `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)`
            WHEN `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` THEN `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `Article 13(3): further processing for another purpose`

-- src:177 | 3. Where the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected, the controller shall provide the data subject prior to that further processing with information on that other purpose and with any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2.
@ref Art 13(3) (src:177)
GIVEN `the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller provided information on that other purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller provided any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was provided prior to that further processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the information on that other purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the relevant further information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 13(3) the controller provides the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected"
        IF (`the controller provided information on that other purpose` OR `the data subject already has the information on that other purpose`)
           AND (`the controller provided any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2` OR `the data subject already has the relevant further information`)
           AND (`the information was provided prior to that further processing` OR (`the data subject already has the information on that other purpose` AND `the data subject already has the relevant further information`))
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall provide the data subject prior to that further processing with information on that other purpose and with any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2"
    -- "any relevant further information": relevance is a judgment; the caller states whether what is relevant was provided.

GIVEN `the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the further processing is to begin` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 13 action`
`Art 13(3) the controller must provide the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information` MEANS
    IF `the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 13(3) provide the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information`
         WITHIN `the time at which the further processing is to begin`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the information was not provided prior to the further processing"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the clock counts from the moment the controller forms the intention; the limit is the instant at which the further processing is to begin ("prior to" is read as at or before that instant: marginal reading, fork F13-2)

§ `Article 13(4): where and insofar as the data subject already has the information`

-- src:178 | 4. Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information.
@ref Art 13(4) (src:178)
GIVEN `the data subject already has the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(4) paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information` MEANS
    IF `the data subject already has the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "shall not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information"
    -- Applied inside `Art 13(1)`, `Art 13(2)` and `Art 13(3)` item by item (the lists of items the data subject already has); this function is the paragraph's question on its own.
